From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Martin=20=C5=A0trobl?= <recordyletsplays@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 01:24:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ANDROID: extcon: s2m: Route D+/D- to USB on the S2MU004

On the Galaxy A3 (2017) the USB data lines pass through the analog
switches of the S2MU004 MUIC. S-Boot leaves them open on a normal boot:
the gadget binds, the port is in device role, and the host sees nothing
(UDC state "not attached", link in suspend). It only worked on the
mainline setup because our U-Boot closes the switches before starting
the kernel; Android is started by S-Boot directly.

Close both switches towards USB when the MUIC is set up, in manual mode
like the vendor driver and U-Boot do.

To be folded into the S2MU004 extcon support of the mainline series.
---
 drivers/extcon/extcon-s2m.c         | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 include/linux/mfd/samsung/s2mu004.h |  7 +++++++
 2 files changed, 26 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/extcon/extcon-s2m.c b/drivers/extcon/extcon-s2m.c
index 812575c799fb..78b99c6347dc 100644
--- a/drivers/extcon/extcon-s2m.c
+++ b/drivers/extcon/extcon-s2m.c
@@ -334,6 +334,25 @@ static int s2mu004_muic_init(struct s2m_muic *priv)
 {
 	int ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * USB D+/D- reach the SoC through the MUIC's switches. The bootloader
+	 * leaves them open on a normal boot, and a host then never sees the
+	 * gadget. Close them towards USB, by hand like the vendor driver.
+	 */
+	ret = regmap_update_bits(priv->regmap, S2MU004_REG_MUIC_SWCTRL,
+				 S2MU004_MUIC_SW_DM | S2MU004_MUIC_SW_DP,
+				 FIELD_PREP(S2MU004_MUIC_SW_DM, S2MU004_MUIC_SW_USB) |
+				 FIELD_PREP(S2MU004_MUIC_SW_DP, S2MU004_MUIC_SW_USB));
+	if (!ret)
+		ret = regmap_update_bits(priv->regmap, S2MU004_REG_MUIC_CTRL1,
+					 S2MU004_MUIC_MANUAL_SW_N |
+					 S2MU004_MUIC_SWITCH_OPEN_N,
+					 S2MU004_MUIC_SWITCH_OPEN_N);
+	if (ret) {
+		dev_err(priv->dev, "failed to route D+/D- to USB\n");
+		return ret;
+	}
+
 	ret = regmap_set_bits(priv->regmap, S2MU004_REG_MUIC_RIDCTRL,
 			      S2MU004_MUIC_RID_ADC_OFF);
 	if (ret) {
diff --git a/include/linux/mfd/samsung/s2mu004.h b/include/linux/mfd/samsung/s2mu004.h
index 93c525603e64..9ea9aa83718e 100644
--- a/include/linux/mfd/samsung/s2mu004.h
+++ b/include/linux/mfd/samsung/s2mu004.h
@@ -140,6 +140,13 @@ enum s2mu004_reg {
 
 /* S2MU004_REG_MUIC_CTRL1 */
 #define S2MU004_MUIC_IRQ_MASK		BIT(0)
+#define S2MU004_MUIC_MANUAL_SW_N	BIT(2)	/* 0: the switches are set by hand */
+#define S2MU004_MUIC_SWITCH_OPEN_N	BIT(4)	/* 0: all switches open */
+
+/* S2MU004_REG_MUIC_SWCTRL */
+#define S2MU004_MUIC_SW_DM		GENMASK(4, 2)
+#define S2MU004_MUIC_SW_DP		GENMASK(7, 5)
+#define S2MU004_MUIC_SW_USB		1
 
 /* S2MU004_REG_MUIC_RIDCTRL */
 #define S2MU004_MUIC_RID_ADC_OFF	BIT(1)
